<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12696"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 06, 2005 - 6:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Future news: <BR>Levenworth, Ks. <BR>The only inmate on Kansas Death Row, convicted BTK serial murderer Dennis Rader was killed today in a prison escape attempt. <BR>Rader had cut the security camera lines in the recreation yard and was hiding in the car trunk of the prison chaplain when the prison&#39;s guard dogs were set loose to search for the escapee. <BR>The dogs soon found Rader and literally ripped him apart. Prison officials said they have never seen anything like it. Prison K9 handler Larry Anderson said &#34;These dogs are trained to subdue the subject until a K9 officer has the subject cuffed and restrained but these dang dogs wouldn&#39;t let up. They just kept chompin&#39; away on the feller.&#34; <BR> Anderson said he was further stunned when apparently a couple of stray dogs from outside the prison snuck through the prison gate and joined in on the carnage. <BR>Most of Rader&#39;s remains will be buried in the prison cemetery. &#34;Were missing an arm and a foot&#34; Anderson explained. &#34;Looks like those stray dogs run off with a couple of pieces.&#34; <BR>Rader was 61.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
